    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0177" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline">CORRESPONDENCE BETWEEN THE DEPARTMENT OF STATE AND THE UNITED
                    STATES CONSULATE GENERAL AT PARIS.</note>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Read to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By cable telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 15, 1870</date>. (Received 5.15 p. m., August
                        15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Paper depreciating daily, also difference between silver and gold; average daily
                    receipts thirteen hundred francs. Very little gold in circulation. What am I to
                    do?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>READ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
